/-!
# Producing the intermediate subalgebra of the factorization into glueings and squishings

The induction of [Stacks, Tag 0C1L] splits a finite morphism `f : X' ⟶ X` with
`𝒪_X ⊂ f_*𝒪_{X'}` by choosing a **finite quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-subalgebra**
`𝒜 ⊂ f_*𝒪_{X'}` and passing to `X' ⟶ Spec_X(𝒜) ⟶ X`. That the two halves of such a splitting
again satisfy the hypotheses of the lemma is
`Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.exists_split_isAlmostIso_of_algebraHom`, which takes `𝒜` as a
hypothesis. This file *produces* `𝒜`, from a single section of `f_*𝒪_{X'}` over an affine open
which the splitting must capture.

## Main results

* `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.isFinite_genSubalg` — **the finiteness of the generated
  subalgebra.** The quasi-coherent subalgebra generated by a finite type quasi-coherent
  submodule of an *integral* algebra sheaf is finite, not merely of finite type. Finiteness of
  `𝒜` is finiteness of `Spec_X(𝒜) ⟶ X`, and finite type would not give it.
* `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.exists_isFinite_subalg_mem` — **the producer.** On a quasi-compact
  and quasi-separated scheme, every section of an integral quasi-coherent algebra sheaf over an
  affine open lies in a finite quasi-coherent subalgebra, presented concretely as a
  `Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.Subalg`.
* `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.exists_split_isAlmostIso_of_section` — **the splitting produced by a
  section.** An almost isomorphism of algebraic `k`-schemes over a quasi-compact quasi-separated
  target splits, with both halves again almost isomorphisms, so that the upper half's sections
  over the preimage of a prescribed affine open `U` contain a prescribed section of
  `f_*𝒪_{X'}` over `U`. A section captured by the intermediate scheme but not by `𝒪_X` witnesses
  `𝒪_X ⊊ q_*𝒪_Z`.

## Implementation notes

The subalgebra is a concrete `Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.Subalg` rather than a
`CategoryTheory.Subobject` as in [Stacks, Tag 0817]
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteSubalgebras.nonempty_isColimit_finiteSubalgebraCocone`): the
hypothesis `hψ` of `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.exists_split_isAlmostIso_of_algebraHom` is
injectivity on the sections over every open, which for a concrete subalgebra is
`Subtype.val_injective`, and the membership statement `s ∈ C.obj U` is literal.

`isFinite_genSubalg` combines
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.isFiniteType_genSubalg` (finite type) with
`Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.IsIntegral.isFinite_of_isFiniteType` ([Stacks, Tag 02JJ] on
affine sections), the subalgebra being integral by
`Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.IsIntegral.of_injective`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C1L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C1L)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0817](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0817)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02JJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02JJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PF)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open Stacks.RelativeSpec Stacks.AffineAlgebraEquivalence
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraGeneratedByModule

universe u

namespace Stacks.GlueSquishFactor

/-! ### Finiteness of the generated subalgebra -/

/-- **The quasi-coherent subalgebra generated by a finite type quasi-coherent submodule of an
integral algebra sheaf is finite.**

This is the finiteness that
`Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.exists_split_isAlmostIso_of_algebraHom` asks of `𝒜`: it is finiteness
of the structure morphism `Spec_X(𝒜) ⟶ X`, so finite type would not do. The subalgebra is of
finite type by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.isFiniteType_genSubalg`, it is integral
because it is a subalgebra of an integral algebra sheaf
(`Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.IsIntegral.of_injective`, whose injectivity hypothesis is
`Subtype.val_injective` for a concrete subalgebra), and integral plus finite type is finite by
[Stacks, Tag 02JJ] on the sections over an affine open. -/
theorem isFinite_genSubalg {X : Scheme.{u}} (A : AlgebraSheaf X)
    [AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A] (hAint : A.IsIntegral)
    (M : (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A).Submodule)
    (hM : Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.IsCompatible
      (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A)
      fun U : X.affineOpens => Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubmoduleGlueOpens.sections M U.1)
    (hMqc : (M.toSheafOfModules : X.Modules).IsQuasicoherent)
    (hMft : (M.toSheafOfModules : X.Modules).IsFiniteType) :
    (AlgebraSheaf.Subalg.toAlgebraSheaf (genSubalg A M hM)).IsFinite :=
  (hAint.of_injective (AlgebraSheaf.Subalg.incl (genSubalg A M hM))
      fun _ => Subtype.val_injective).isFinite_of_isFiniteType
    (isFiniteType_genSubalg A M hM hMqc hMft)

/-! ### The producer -/

/-- **The subalgebra producer of [Stacks, Tag 0C1L].** On a quasi-compact and quasi-separated
scheme, every section of an integral quasi-coherent sheaf of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras over an
affine open lies in a *finite* quasi-coherent subalgebra.

The subalgebra is the one generated by a finite type quasi-coherent submodule containing the
section, which [Stacks, Tag 01PF] supplies
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.exists_submodule_mem_of_qcqs`), and the
subalgebra it generates is quasi-coherent, finite, and contains the section over the given
affine open. It is produced as a concrete
`Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.Subalg`, so that the inclusion into `A` is injective on the
sections over every open by `Subtype.val_injective`. -/
@[ega "IV 8.12.3" "more general"]
theorem exists_isFinite_subalg_mem {X : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (A : AlgebraSheaf X) [AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A] (hAint : A.IsIntegral)
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (s : A.right.obj.obj (op U)) :
    ∃ C : AlgebraSheaf.Subalg A,
      (AlgebraSheaf.Subalg.toAlgebraSheaf C).IsQuasicoherent ∧
        (AlgebraSheaf.Subalg.toAlgebraSheaf C).IsFinite ∧ s ∈ C.obj U := by
  obtain ⟨M, hMqc, hMft, hsM⟩ :=
    exists_submodule_mem_of_qcqs (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A) ⟨U, hU⟩ s
  have hM := isCompatible_sections (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A) M hMqc
  exact ⟨genSubalg A M hM, isQuasicoherent_genSubalg A M hM,
    isFinite_genSubalg A hAint M hM hMqc hMft,
    (mem_genSubalg_obj_iff A M hM ⟨U, hU⟩ s).mpr (mem_adjoinSubmodule_of_mem A hsM)⟩

/-! ### The splitting produced by a section -/

/-- **The splitting step of [Stacks, Tag 0C1L], produced by a section.** Let `f : X' ⟶ X` be an
almost isomorphism of algebraic `k`-schemes with `X` quasi-compact and quasi-separated, let `U`
be an affine open of `X` and let `s` be a section of `f_*𝒪_{X'}` over `U`. Then `f` factors over
`Spec k` as `p ≫ q` with both halves again almost isomorphisms, and `s` is a section of the
intermediate scheme: it is in the image of `𝒪_Z(q⁻¹U) ⟶ 𝒪_{X'}(f⁻¹U)`.

The subalgebra `𝒜` of `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.exists_split_isAlmostIso_of_algebraHom` is
produced from `s` by `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.exists_isFinite_subalg_mem`. -/
theorem exists_split_isAlmostIso_of_section {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    {X' X : Over (Spec (.of k))} [CompactSpace X.left] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X.left]
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (hf : IsAlmostIso f) {U : X.left.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (s : Γ(X'.left, f.left ⁻¹ᵁ U)) :
    ∃ (Z : Over (Spec (.of k))) (p : X' ⟶ Z) (q : Z ⟶ X),
      p ≫ q = f ∧ IsAlmostIso q ∧ IsAlmostIso p ∧
        ∀ hle : f.left ⁻¹ᵁ U ≤ p.left ⁻¹ᵁ (q.left ⁻¹ᵁ U),
          s ∈ Set.range (p.left.appLE (q.left ⁻¹ᵁ U) (f.left ⁻¹ᵁ U) hle).hom := by
  have hffin : IsFinite f.left := hf.1.2.2.2.2.1
  have hAint : (pushforwardAlgebra f.left).IsIntegral :=
    (AlgebraicGeometry.isFinite_pushforwardAlgebra f.left).isIntegral
  obtain ⟨C, hCqc, hCfin, hsC⟩ :=
    exists_isFinite_subalg_mem (pushforwardAlgebra f.left) hAint hU s
  have := hCqc
  obtain ⟨Z, p, q, hpq, hq, hp, hcap⟩ :=
    exists_split_isAlmostIso_of_algebraHom f hf (AlgebraSheaf.Subalg.toAlgebraSheaf C) hCfin
      (AlgebraSheaf.Subalg.incl C) fun _ => Subtype.val_injective
  exact ⟨Z, p, q, hpq, hq, hp, fun hle => hcap U hle s ⟨⟨s, hsC⟩, rfl⟩⟩

end Stacks.GlueSquishFactor

end
